part invest
  tally 1
  note "Fund units and their tax. Lots are matched to sales first in, first out within their account (PIT-8 .3); a sale's gain is its proceeds less its fee and the cost of the units it took (.2); a gain on units held more than 5 years is left out (.6), a gifted lot counting from the giver's acquisition; a person's year adds up (.4); a year's loss is carried 5 years, at most half of it in a year, older first (.5). The wrapped account's withdrawal (PIT-9 .4, .5). The 15th (A-HR1, A-HR2) read from the joint account's records (A-09)."
  note "One lot input holds lots of several funds, so every fund's units are one unit, fund_u (observation O:A-4)."

input inv_holder[x in place]: key spouse question "In whose name is this fund account (PIT-8, PIT-9)?"

